      "de Wet, C. (2013) 'Cecil Wele Manona 1937–2013', Anthropology Southern Africa, 37(1). doi: 10.1080/23323256.2014.940196.",
      "ECRDA (2022) Magwa Tea Estate. Eastern Cape Rural Development Agency. Available at: ecrda.co.za.",
      "Evans, L. (2013) 'Gender, generation and the experiences of farm dwellers resettled in the Ciskei Bantustan, South Africa, ca 1960–1976', Journal of Agrarian Change, 13(2), pp. 213–233.",
      "Fischer, K., Hajdu, M. and Johnson, K. (2024) 'Social drivers and differentiated effects of deagrarianisation: A longitudinal study of smallholder farming in South Africa's Eastern Cape province', Journal of Rural Studies, 107, 103200. doi: 10.1016/j.jrurstud.2024.103200.",
      "Grocott's Mail (2010) 'Glenmore — the story of the forgotten', Grocott's Mail, 19 August. Available at: grocotts.ru.ac.za.",
      "Harrison, P. (1988) The Magwa Tea Venture: A Case Study. Unpublished report. Johannesburg: University of the Witwatersrand.",
      "Maclennan, B. (1979) Glenmore: The Story of a Forced Removal. Grahamstown: Grahamstown Rural Committee.",
      "Magwa Tea (2019) Magwa and Majola Black Tea: Tea Estate and Tea Supplier Eastern Cape. Available at: magwatea.com.",
      "Manona, C.W. (1987) 'Land tenure in an urban area', Development Southern Africa, 4(1), pp. 1–15. doi: 10.1080/03768358708439344.",
      "Manona, C.W. (1988) 'Impact of urbanization on rural areas: The case of white-owned farms in the Eastern Cape', African Studies, 47(1), pp. 1–18. doi: 10.1080/00020188808707684.",
      "Manona, C.W. (1995) Gender, Households and Environmental Changes in Informal Settlements in the Eastern Cape Province, South Africa. Development Studies Working Paper No. 64. Grahamstown: Institute of Social and Economic Research, Rhodes University.",
      "Manona, C.W. (1998a) 'The virtual collapse of agriculture in a former Ciskei community', Africa Insight, 28(3–4), pp. 160–166.",
      "Manona, C.W. (1998b) 'Land tenure and use: Perspectives from a village in the Eastern Cape, South Africa', African Sociological Review, 2(2), pp. 77–89. Available at: jstor.org/stable/24487431.",
      "Manona, C.W. (1999) De-agrarianisation and the Urbanisation of a Rural Economy: Agrarian Patterns in Melani Village in the Eastern Cape. Leiden: African Studies Centre, Leiden University.",
      "Manona, C.W. and Manona, N. (1997) Situational Analysis of Magwa. Commissioned by the Department of Land Affairs. Grahamstown: Institute of Social and Economic Research, Rhodes University.",
      "Mills, M.E. and Wilson, M. (1952) Keiskammahoek Rural Survey, Vol. 3: Land Tenure. Pietermaritzburg: Shuter and Shooter.",
      "Porter, C. and Phillips-Howard, K. (1996) The Magwa Tea Venture: A Review. Unpublished report. Johannesburg: University of the Witwatersrand.",
      "Rhodes University (2013b) 'End of road for \"humble, bright rural boy\"', Rhodes University Latest News, October 2013. Available at: ru.ac.za.",
      "South African History Online (2016) 'Representations on the Glenmore removals', South African History Online, 22 February. Available at: sahistory.org.za.",
      "Sullivan, L. (1977) The Sullivan Principles: Code of Conduct for U.S. Corporations Operating in South Africa. Philadelphia: Sullivan Foundation.",
      "Whisson, M. (2013a) 'Rhodes University bids farewell to a brave and generous spirited scholar', Rhodes University Latest News, October 2013. Available at: ru.ac.za.",
